Qore V8 module packages
=======================

This development snapshot targets qore-testing, not general release. The
runtime contains native bindings, TypeScriptProxy/TypeScriptActionInterface
AOT modules, two tools and metadata. Its exact-version common package provides
source modules, resources and all qlib catalogs.
The doc package contains three API references and test examples.

Tracked container-build artifacts are excluded and all binaries are rebuilt.
The separately built ts/ app catalogue is excluded from the +ds source archive.
It needs its own offline npm dependency and third-party schema license inventory.
No npm install or network download occurs during these package builds. The bridge
and user-supplied apps work without this optional catalogue. Configure an app
script with QORE_TYPESCRIPT_MASTER_ACTION_SCRIPT or QORE_TYPESCRIPT_ACTION_SCRIPTS.
Catalog-derived qlib translations are retained for those apps. The offline
build checks complete locale/message/source parity against their committed
roots; current app ownership and regenerated-root qualification require the
separately built catalogue and are not claimed by this bridge-only package.

Use dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc with the matching Qore 3 SDK, packaged process/uuid
modules, libnode-dev and node-typescript. Ubuntu's Node exposes stripTypeScriptTypes
but disables its built-in compiler; TypeScriptProgram uses node-typescript in that
case. QORE_TYPESCRIPT_MODULE selects the compiler name/path at CMake configure
time; packaging sets its absolute distribution path so standalone qcc executables
work regardless of their own directory. It preserves ES module syntax, reports syntax diagnostics, and never treats
other transpilation/runtime errors as an unavailable compiler.

Full, arch-only, indep-only, nocheck and nodoc profiles build offline. Cross builds
need a separate host SDK and are explicitly rejected. Fixed qcc partitions,
ordered sibling modules and preserved AOT trailers support reproducibility.
Tests use loopback fixtures and synthetic Google Discovery metadata. The optional
HubSpot OAuth suite explicitly skips when its matching built catalogue is absent;
separate qualification must supply its matching rest.js fixture and dependencies.
Eight fault-injection cases explicitly skip for release AOT modules, where their
debug hooks are compiled out; source-mode qualification executes these cases. A
real child-exit/restart test runs in both modes without debug hooks.
Runtime/compiler autopkgtests exclude checkout module paths. Supplement these
with source-mode, teardown, resource/locale, debug and install/purge/reinstall checks.

Before general publication, freeze the Qore ABI, qualify other Debian/Ubuntu
releases and architectures, and test relevant upgrades. No previous module package
is available for upgrade tests. Testing PPA publication needs the matching
published SDK and process/uuid packages, source signing and upload.
